et connections without any authentication. By opening a large number of simultaneous connections, an attacker can exhaust server resources\u2014such as memory, CPU, and file descriptors\u2014leading to a complete denial of service for legitimate users.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a vulnerability was identified in the feast feature server's `/ws/chat` endpoint that allows remote attackers to establish persistent websocket connections without any authentication. by opening a large number of simultaneous connections, an attacker can exhaust server resources\u2014such as memory, cpu, and file descriptors\u2014leading to a complete denial of service for legitimate users."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"product","object":"Feast Feature Server","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast feature server"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift ai (rhoai)"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-770","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-770"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"vendor","object":"Feast","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"feast"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-23538","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"}]